Lindsay Hyde studied with me. We had one-on-one tutorial as well. We worked a lot together.

571
01:13:01,540 --> 01:13:04,440
Lindsay Hyde is the founder of Strong Women, Strong Girls.

572
01:13:05,560 --> 01:13:16,620
Wonderful organization, part of PBHA. She founded it now, a national organization. I was also one of the founding board members of that organization.

573
01:13:16,900 --> 01:13:26,620
Wonderful stuff, swsg.org, for those of you interested. And I was invited by Lindsay to give a talk for strong women, strong girls,

574
01:13:26,820 --> 01:13:29,660
for the mentors who were Harvard students,

575
01:13:30,560 --> 01:13:34,440
as well as students from other women from other colleges around Boston.

576
01:13:35,280 --> 01:13:38,220
And I gave a talk, and here is Lindsay.

577
01:13:38,220 --> 01:13:48,500
Here she is with one of the students, third grade student, whom she mentors and other Harvard students mentor and do wonderful work. And I believe in this organization.

578
01:13:48,500 --> 01:13:51,540
I support it from the get-go almost.

579
01:13:54,180 --> 01:14:08,320
And I gave a talk, and the talk was about teaching the importance of role modeling, was about integrity, talked to them about Marvel Collins, and about the important work that they were doing.

580
01:14:09,460 --> 01:14:16,900
and at the end of the talk which went well I think for myself for the participants I got a present

581
01:14:17,440 --> 01:14:21,280
a gift, a token of appreciation and the present was a shirt

582
01:14:22,180 --> 01:14:26,900
it wasn't any shirt it was a pink shirt

583
01:14:27,520 --> 01:14:32,320
a color I don't normally wear certainly never wore it in Israel

584
01:14:34,040 --> 01:14:45,220
not only was it a pink shirt it was, since it was a strong women, strong girls shirt It was also a very small shirt, more suited for the third graders than for older ones.

585
01:14:45,300 --> 01:14:48,700
But still, they said, we want you to have it as a token of our appreciation.

586
01:14:49,360 --> 01:14:50,840
And then I made a mistake.

587
01:14:51,320 --> 01:15:02,100
And I said, jokingly, of course, I was teaching 1504 at the time. I said, jokingly, I will wear the shirt to class and laughed.

588
01:15:03,320 --> 01:15:06,060
And here it is, the shirt that I got.

589
01:15:08,360 --> 01:15:18,600
And then there was another student of mine from 1504, Tori Martin, who ran the organization at that time, took over from Lindsay at Harvard.

590
01:15:19,060 --> 01:15:22,640
And Tori Martin said, I'm going to hold you to it.

591
01:15:23,900 --> 01:15:26,020
And I laughed and then almost cried.

592
01:15:28,280 --> 01:15:38,780
What do you mean, hold me to it? I mean, I was joking. She said, look, you just talked to us about the importance of integrity, which I did. I mean, look here, integrity, it's even behind.

593
01:15:39,820 --> 01:15:40,660
I did.

594
01:15:43,210 --> 01:15:48,610
And I said, that's right, I did. So what, am I going to go back on my word? That's one of my core values, integrity.

595
01:15:49,450 --> 01:15:53,150
And then my whole childhood flashed before my eyes.

596
01:15:54,270 --> 01:16:02,850
And I thought about something that Churchill said, which was, find opportunity in difficulty.

597
01:16:04,830 --> 01:16:14,390
So I looked for the opportunity. And here was an opportunity handed to me in a pink shirt to be more in touch with my feminine side.

598
01:16:14,690 --> 01:16:19,590
So, ladies and gentlemen, spring fashion 2008.

599
01:16:20,330 --> 01:17:25,630
Sorry, Barry.

600
01:17:29,650 --> 01:17:33,150
Now, I know you're going to find this hard to believe.

601
01:17:34,370 --> 01:17:40,330
But believe me when I say that this for me was going out of my comfort zone.

602
01:17:44,900 --> 01:17:54,640
In fact, maybe it was going out of my stretch zone a little bit. but into my panic zone. I was telling the TFs before class that when I prepare for this class

603
01:17:54,640 --> 01:18:00,900
and I have all my notes here and I write, every time I went over it or when I initially wrote it on my notes,

604
01:18:00,900 --> 01:18:12,000
it was like an adrenaline rush in my stomach going out of my comfort zone. Now, I'm also out of my comfort zone, which is why I had to have it at the end of the class

605
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:13,940
as opposed to the beginning of class.

606
01:18:15,540 --> 01:18:20,700
but the key is to attain optimum levels of discomfort i may have overshot a little bit

607
01:18:20,700 --> 01:18:29,360
but the key is optimum levels of discomfort and why there is no other way to change i can think

608
01:18:29,360 --> 01:18:35,060
about it all day long and say i want to be in touch with my family side or i want to be more

609
01:18:35,060 --> 01:18:42,140
courageous i want to get up i can think about it all day long nothing will happen nothing will

610
01:18:42,140 --> 01:18:49,760
happen unless we bring about real actual behavioral change, real actual

611
01:18:49,760 --> 01:18:57,620
behavioral action. And when we do that, then the sky's the limit. Thank you. I will see you on Thursday.
